<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's Sept oil output fell 0.8 pct from yr ago.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's Sept oil output fell 0.8 pct from yr ago.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador produced an average of 384,526 barrels per day (bpd) of crude oil in September, down 0.8 percent from the 387,592 pumped in same month last year, an official said Thursday.</p>
<p>An official from National Petroleum Office, who asked not to be identified, said average output in the first nine months was 383,313 bpd. A comparitive figure was not available.</p>
<p>Oil production averaged 386,706 bpd last year.</p>
<p>--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
</text>
